  "title": "The Forest Mends Its Path",
  "mood": "Quiet damp woodland; a deliberate living-wood crossing",
  "reason": "Compared a lowering root bridge, a closing fern canopy, and a walking grove. Bridge connects image01's rust-earth passage with image02's interlocking pale mossy limbs; canopy lacks a journey and walking trees weaken attachment credibility. Invent a hinged fallen-tree crossing: raised opening, slow descent, settled passage. Banks, foreground roots and layered trees establish a ravine rather than an isolated ornament.",
